 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "All of it lives in `src/tessel/views.py`, in two classes: `View` and its subclass `VerbView`.\n\n**Class-based view to view function**\n- `View.to_view_func(name, ...)` (`views.py:86`) is a classmethod that builds a plain `view(**kwargs)` function.\n- By default each request instantiates the class and calls `self.run_view(**kwargs)` through `active_app.ensure_sync`.\n- If `init_every_request = False`, one shared instance is used instead.\n- The function is named after `name` and gets the class's `decorators` applied.\n- It also gets `view_class`, `methods` and `provide_automatic_options` attributes copied from the class (`views.py:133-134`).\n- Route registration reads those attributes, so the URL rule is limited to the right HTTP methods.\n\n**Routing to `get()` / `post()`**\n- `VerbView.__init_subclass__` (`views.py:165`) sets `cls.methods` automatically. It collects `GET`, `POST` and so on for each lowercase method defined on the class, plus any `methods` inherited from base classes.\n- `VerbView.run_view` (`views.py:182`) does `getattr(self, request.method.lower())` and calls that handler. A `HEAD` request falls back to `get()` if there's no `head()`.",
